  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1254 PM MDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nA drying trend will occur mid-week as the monsoon high re-centers \nitself over the TX Panhandle and eventually directly over central NM \nby late week. The best rain chances will be over western NM \nWednesday, then over northern NM Thursday and Friday as the \ndisturbance currently over southern NM rotates clockwise around the \nupper high. The ridge will amplify over the southern Rockies this \nweekend so moisture in place will continue to be recycled. Both the \nGEFS and ENS ensemble means suggest PWATs will be near to slightly \nabove normal across most of New Mexico, which should be sufficient \nfor at least scattered afternoon showers and storms. With the ridge \noverhead, storm motions will trend slower late week into the \nweekend, which will keep most storms over the mountains and increase \nthe risk of burn scar flash flooding.",
